    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d253">

                <pb facs="0576" n="440" sameAs="frus:frus1929v01/pg440"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.554/8</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Belgium</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Reed</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Brussels</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-04-29">April 29, 1929</date>.<lb/>[Received May
                        11.]</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 433</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to transmit herewith a
                    copy and English translation of a note from the Foreign Office dated April 27,
                    1929, which contains the Belgian Government’s reply to the suggestions looking
                    toward the conclusion of conventions respecting dual nationality and compulsory
                    military service, which the Embassy made in compliance with the Department’s
                    instruction No. 167 of December 1, 1928.</p>
                <p>It will be noted that the Belgian Government, for reasons set forth in this
                    communication, is not convinced of the necessity for entering into agreements of
                    the nature proposed by the Department, but is nevertheless entirely disposed to
                    carry the discussions further, should the Department so desire.<anchor n="5"
                        xml:id="d253-f1"/></p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Edward L. Reed</hi></signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d253-a1.xml" xpointer="d253-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d253-f1" n="5" xml:id="d253-f1-content">
                <p>Negotiations for the conclusion of a convention do not appear to have been
                    continued.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
